    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948420,
    "guid": "524C42009DCC11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948398,
    "previous_guid": "BAC0EE409DBC11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Gently wash the cells with PBS (see Table 1, column B for recommended volume). Aspirate the PBS from the flask.\n\nAlways aim to add reagents at the side/back of the flask initially to avoid dislodging any cells.\n \n\n<table class=\"component-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n%s</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n%s\n</tbody>\n</table>\r\n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "2",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948421,
    "guid": "31B58E609DCD11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948420,
    "previous_guid": "524C42009DCC11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Add sufficient TrypLE Express Enzyme to cover the bottom of the flask (see Table 1, column C for recommended volume). Rock the flask to allow the TrypLE to cover the surface of the cells.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "3",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948422,
    "guid": "F4D333C09DCD11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948421,
    "previous_guid": "31B58E609DCD11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Incubate the flask at  37 \u00b0C   for 3-5 minutes. Use the microscope to check if the cells have detached. If necessary, tap the side of the flask, or return to incubator until all cells have detached.\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "4",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948423,
    "guid": "E02D99509DCE11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948422,
    "previous_guid": "F4D333C09DCD11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Add fresh media to the flask at an equal volume to the TrypLE added in Step 3. Use the liquid in the flask to rinse the cells off the bottom of the flask. Transfer the entire volume to an appropriately sized sterile tube. ",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "5",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948424,
    "guid": "7DD16F109DCF11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948423,
    "previous_guid": "E02D99509DCE11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Spin the tube at {\"centrifuge\":\"300\",\"duration\":0,\"guid\":\"94C4AD909DCF11EA814529A47F98D72C\",\"id\":0,\"label\":\"\",\"pause\":null,\"preset\":[],\"start\":null,\"temperature\":\"\",\"temperatureUnit\":10,\"unit\":34}  for 3 minutes. \n\nTubes should be spun inside centrifuge buckets with sealed safety caps. After spinning, the sealed bucket should be transferred to a microbiology safety cabinet before removing the tubes.\n \n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "6",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948425,
    "guid": "579D33A09DD011EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948424,
    "previous_guid": "7DD16F109DCF11EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Aspirate the supernatant, taking care to avoid disturbing the cell pellet. Resuspend the pellet in an appropriate volume of fresh media (around  5 mL  - 20 mL  ) and mix well to ensure a single cell suspension.\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "7",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 948426,
    "guid": "D144D9109DD011EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "previous_id": 948425,
    "previous_guid": "579D33A09DD011EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Detaching and collecting cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "If a cell count is **not required**, proceed to Step 9. \nTo take a cell count, aliquot  100 \u00b5L  of cell suspension and count using your preferred method.\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 974865,
    "guid": "35D32D90BFA611EA922DB5E06021B5E1",
    "previous_id": 948426,
    "previous_guid": "D144D9109DD011EA814529A47F98D72C",
    "section": "<p>Re-seeding cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Add fresh media and an appropriate volume of cell suspension to a new flask, to achieve the desired split ratio or cell number (where possible, aim for the total volume of media and cells in the flask to follow the recommeded volumes in Table 1, column D). \n\nFor example, **if splitting a T75 flask 1:2, either** add the entire cell suspension to fresh media in a T150 flask (achieving a total volume of  24 mL  ), **OR** add half the cell suspension to fresh media in a T75 (achieving a total volume of  12 mL  ).\n\n\nThe required split ratio will be dependend on the growth rate and behaviour of individual cell lines.\n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 37443,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "9",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 974866,
    "guid": "91FDB0E0BFA611EA922DB5E06021B5E1",
    "previous_id": 974865,
    "previous_guid": "35D32D90BFA611EA922DB5E06021B5E1",
    "section": "<p>Re-seeding cells</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": true,
    "step": "**If maintaining a selected population of Cas9 cells**, add blasticidin to achieve the desired concentration, as determined by: &#39;Blasticidin titration of cancer cell lines&#39; protocol. \n\nAdd the required volume of 10mg/ml blasticidin depending on the flask size (Table 2), to achieve the desired final concentration.\n\n<table class=\"component-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n%s</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n%s\n</tbody>\n</table>\r\n \n\n\nBlasticidin is toxic if swallowed and harmful in contact with skin.\n \n",
    "data": null,
